const GLOSSARY = [
["Left and right","Terms from the French Revolution: supporters of the king sat on the right of the assembly, supporters of change on the left. Today they mostly describe economic views."],
["Political compass","A chart with two or more axes. The idea goes back to Hans Eysenck (1950s) and David Nolan (1969); the version with an economic and an authority axis became popular online after 2001."],
["Libertarian","Wanting less state power over individuals. On the left it means anarchism and self-management; on the right, free markets with a minimal state."],
["Authoritarian","Wanting a strong state that enforces order, often at the cost of civil liberties."],
["Progressive","Favouring changes in values and law that widen rights and equality."],
["Traditionalist","Favouring inherited values, institutions and ways of life."],
["Socialism","Social or worker ownership of the means of production. Covers a wide range, from revolutionary to parliamentary."],
["Capitalism","An economy based on private ownership, wage labour and production for profit in markets."],
["Anarchism","The view that the state, and other unjustified hierarchy, should be abolished."],
["Fascism","An authoritarian nationalism of the 1920s–40s that aimed at national rebirth through a one-party state."],
["Liberalism","Individual rights, limited government and the rule of law. In the US the word often means centre-left; in Europe it often means pro-market."],
["Conservatism","Defending established institutions and preferring slow change."],
["Vanguard party","Lenin's idea of a disciplined party of committed revolutionaries leading the working class."],
["Subsidiarity","Decisions should be taken at the most local level that can handle them. Central to Christian Democracy and the EU."],
["Welfare state","A state that provides healthcare, pensions, unemployment support and similar services to all citizens."],
["Nationalisation","Bringing a private company or industry into public ownership."],
];

